{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wompc66q6vxWk8MYGKovRH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ADR-012: Form-associated custom elements\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-11-24\n4\t\n5\t**Status:** Accepted\n6\t\n7\t**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size)\n8\t\n9\t## Context\n10\t\n11\tA component author who wants to build a form control (a custom input,\n12\ta rich text field, a rating widget) cannot make it a real form control\n13\twith microtags. The platform way is a form-associated custom element:\n14\tthe class sets a static `formAssociated = true`, each host gets an\n15\t`ElementInternals` from `attachInternals()`, and the browser wires it\n16\tinto the containing form for submission, validation, and disabled\n17\tstate. Microtags calls `customElements.define` inside `setup()` with\n18\tno way to set the static first, and does not expose\n19\t`ElementInternals` to the setup callback.\n20\t\n21\tThe first consumer is `markdown-area`, a `<textarea>` replacement.\n22\t\n23\t## Decision\n24\t\n25\tA new builder link, `.formAssociated()`, opts a component into the\n26\tplatform's form-associated custom element behaviour. It takes no\n27\targuments.\n28\t\n29\t- **Builder link.** `.formAssociated()` returns a new builder with an\n30\t  internal `formAssociated` flag. The flag propagates through all\n31\t  subsequent links. It composes with `withProps`, `withRefs`,\n32\t  `withContexts` and `render` in any order.\n33\t\n34\t- **Static.** The factory sets `static formAssociated = true` on the\n35\t  generated class before the builder calls `customElements.define`,\n36\t  so the browser reads it at define time.\n37\t\n38\t- **Internals.** A form-associated host calls `attachInternals()`\n39\t  once, in its constructor. The result is kept on the instance and\n40\t  reused across disconnect/reconnect cycles. Setup receives it as\n41\t  `ctx.internals`.\n42\t\n43\t- **Setup context.** For a form-associated component the setup context\n44\t  gains `internals:ElementInternals`. Components that did not opt in\n45\t  get a type error when they read `ctx.internals`.\n46\t\n47\t- **Form lifecycle callbacks.** Planned for ticket 03. The class will\n48\t  install `formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`,\n49\t  `formStateRestoreCallback` and `formAssociatedCallback` on the\n50\t  prototype, each forwarding to handlers registered through a\n51\t  `ctx.form(handlers)` method. The `restore` callback is replayed\n52\t  when a handler is registered; the others are not (their state is\n53\t  readable from the host and `internals`).\n54\t\n55\t- **Server render.** `render-support` is unchanged: form association\n56\t  has no server-side meaning.\n57\t\n58\t- **Types.** `FormAssociatedContext` is a public type export from\n59\t  `microtags`, so declaration emit in consuming packages does not hit\n60\t  TS2883. The builder carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter that\n61\t  controls whether the setup context includes `internals`.\n62\t\n63\t## Size cost\n64\t\n65\t| Entry | Before | After | Delta |\n66\t|-------|--------|-------|-------|\n67\t| `microtags` (core) | 4.04 kB | 4.09 kB | +50 B |\n68\t\n69\tThe 50 B delta is well under the 150 B target from the spec. It\n70\tcovers the `formAssociated` static, the `attachInternals()` call in\n71\tthe constructor, and passing internals to the setup context.\n72\t\n73\t## Consequences\n74\t\n75\t- Authors can build form controls that submit values, participate in\n76\t  constraint validation, follow `disabled` from ancestor fieldsets,\n77\t  and hear about form reset and state restore (once ticket 03 lands).\n78\t- Components that do not opt in pay no runtime cost and no API change.\n79\t- The core entry limit rises from 4.1 kB to 4.15 kB.\n80\t\n81\t[adr-004]: ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b493dbd6-6389-478a-b86a-02c93f0db15a","uuid":"b2dda274-a3c3-4da1-af24-89385da9084b","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:43:50.711Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.form-associated-03-form-lifecycle-handlers/docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md","content":"# ADR-012: Form-associated custom elements\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-24\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size)\n\n## Context\n\nA component author who wants to build a form control (a custom input,\na rich text field, a rating widget) cannot make it a real form control\nwith microtags. The platform way is a form-associated custom element:\nthe class sets a static `formAssociated = true`, each host gets an\n`ElementInternals` from `attachInternals()`, and the browser wires it\ninto the containing form for submission, validation, and disabled\nstate. Microtags calls `customElements.define` inside `setup()` with\nno way to set the static first, and does not expose\n`ElementInternals` to the setup callback.\n\nThe first consumer is `markdown-area`, a `<textarea>` replacement.\n\n## Decision\n\nA new builder link, `.formAssociated()`, opts a component into the\nplatform's form-associated custom element behaviour. It takes no\narguments.\n\n- **Builder link.** `.formAssociated()` returns a new builder with an\n  internal `formAssociated` flag. The flag propagates through all\n  subsequent links. It composes with `withProps`, `withRefs`,\n  `withContexts` and `render` in any order.\n\n- **Static.** The factory sets `static formAssociated = true` on the\n  generated class before the builder calls `customElements.define`,\n  so the browser reads it at define time.\n\n- **Internals.** A form-associated host calls `attachInternals()`\n  once, in its constructor. The result is kept on the instance and\n  reused across disconnect/reconnect cycles. Setup receives it as\n  `ctx.internals`.\n\n- **Setup context.** For a form-associated component the setup context\n  gains `internals:ElementInternals`. Components that did not opt in\n  get a type error when they read `ctx.internals`.\n\n- **Form lifecycle callbacks.** Planned for ticket 03. The class will\n  install `formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`,\n  `formStateRestoreCallback` and `formAssociatedCallback` on the\n  prototype, each forwarding to handlers registered through a\n  `ctx.form(handlers)` method. The `restore` callback is replayed\n  when a handler is registered; the others are not (their state is\n  readable from the host and `internals`).\n\n- **Server render.** `render-support` is unchanged: form association\n  has no server-side meaning.\n\n- **Types.** `FormAssociatedContext` is a public type export from\n  `microtags`, so declaration emit in consuming packages does not hit\n  TS2883. The builder carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter that\n  controls whether the setup context includes `internals`.\n\n## Size cost\n\n| Entry | Before | After | Delta |\n|-------|--------|-------|-------|\n| `microtags` (core) | 4.04 kB | 4.09 kB | +50 B |\n\nThe 50 B delta is well under the 150 B target from the spec. It\ncovers the `formAssociated` static, the `attachInternals()` call in\nthe constructor, and passing internals to the setup context.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Authors can build form controls that submit values, participate in\n  constraint validation, follow `disabled` from ancestor fieldsets,\n  and hear about form reset and state restore (once ticket 03 lands).\n- Components that do not opt in pay no runtime cost and no API change.\n- The core entry limit rises from 4.1 kB to 4.15 kB.\n\n[adr-004]: ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n","numLines":82,"startLine":1,"totalLines":82}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wompc66q6vxWk8MYGKovRH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
